    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "08325421_3c9dfe47",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/NetworkAgent.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1012,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-07T08:53:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "FWIW I don\u0027t think this provides much value.\n\n- The set of callers of this API is small enough that it\u0027s probably fine if we simply ignore invalid values being passed in, like we do if the caller attempts to change the owner UID.\n- There is already lots of sanitization of networkcapabilities going on, and this code duplicates that.\n- Further, some of that sanitization may not even be possible in app space because it might require data that is only available in CS at runtime (for example, this method cannot implement the previously-mentioned \"ignore owner UID changes\" sanitization because the previous owner is not known to this method (and not even known to this class, because this class does not remember previously-sent capabilities). It also cannot reliably implement a \"only the carrier privileged app can be in the access UIDs restriction\", because there is a race between when this code can check the carrier privileged app and when CS checks it.\n- Even though you have a comment in line 1009, the presence of this code might cause folks to think that this method can somehow guarantee that CS doesn\u0027t get any invalid input. This isn\u0027t possible due to the point above.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1012,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 1012,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "9dbf1d39407f337abf2ca4d3e1ea50467cdecc67",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e959a8b0_f9b0b7ea",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1800,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-07T08:53:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Related to the comment below about performance... do we expect that it\u0027s useful for this to be a set of *ranges*, as opposed to being a set of *UIDs*? The UIDs in this object are primarily used for the VPN APIs, and in those ranges are quite common: they\u0027re used to represent \"a whole user profile\" or \"a whole user profile minus a few excluded UIDs\". That doesn\u0027t seem to be the case here.\n\nIf we expect that this will primarily be used to allow access to a given network for only a few UIDs, then this would perform better if it was a Set\u003cInteger\u003e or even a SparseBooleanArray. We don\u0027t have to make these performance implementations in this CL, but if we unhide Builder#setAccessUids in its current form that takes a Set\u003cUidRange\u003e, then we will not be able to change the implementation in the future.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1800,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 1800,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "9dbf1d39407f337abf2ca4d3e1ea50467cdecc67",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "39652385_7820b5d2",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/NetworkCapabilities.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1845,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-07T08:53:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is moderately expensive, involving creating a copy of mAccessUids. NetworkCapabilities#equals is probably called quite frequently. Can we do better? Perhaps by using a better structure such as a sorted set? Or by making the access UIDs only a set of UIDs, not a set of UID ranges?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1845,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 1845,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "9dbf1d39407f337abf2ca4d3e1ea50467cdecc67",
